    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0498" n="394" xml:id="pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-13T13:00:00-03:00">July 13, 1932—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 13—12:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. At the request of the Government the All America Cables has disconnected its
                    cable at Montevideo in order to prevent its use by São Paulo authorities in
                    control of the Santos Station.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
